{
 "provenance": {
  "source": "hand-authored",
  "date": "2026-09-06",
  "evidence": "AWS Signature Version 4 test suite, vendored verbatim in botocore (tests/unit/auth/aws4_testsuite), frozen under research/cloud-hosts/sources/aws-sigv4-suite/ with sha256 in research/cloud-hosts/sources/manifest.json; changes/2026-09-03-cloud-hosts.md; spec/auth.md AUTH-11. Transcribed mechanically from the .req/.creq/.sts/.authz files; the request line, headers and body are the suite's bytes. 2026-09-06 (D15, verify/DECISIONS-2026-09-06.md; ratified by Maxime Rivest 2026-09-06): the complete suite — all 34 case directories that carry .req/.creq/.sts/.authz — fetched 2026-09-07 from botocore's default branch `develop` (there is no `main`) at commit b4c8dd94e3e705217ee084e84dbb6aa747417c8b, frozen flat under research/cloud-hosts/sources/aws-sigv4-suite/ (the ten cases frozen 2026-09-03 re-fetched byte-identical). Transcription rule, applied mechanically to every case: request line -> method + target verbatim (raw space, UTF-8, `$`, dot segments and pre-encoded bytes kept as the file has them); header lines -> name and the text after the first colon, verbatim (leading whitespace kept); a repeated header name -> a list of its values in file order; a folded continuation line -> appended to the previous value with the newline kept; the text after the first blank line -> body; .creq/.sts/.authz -> expect, verbatim. get-vanilla-with-session-token carries `session_token` at the case level: its .req has no X-Amz-Security-Token header, yet its .creq signs one, so the token comes from the credential. Cases the reference signer fails are reported in harness/reports, never dropped (AUTHORITY.md)."
 },
 "description": "SigV4 signing vectors (AUTH-11): the complete AWS Signature Version 4 test suite, 34 cases. Fixed inputs for every case: access key AKIDEXAMPLE, secret wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG+bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY, region us-east-1, service 'service', clock 2015-08-30T12:36:00Z, host example.amazonaws.com. A port's signer must reproduce canonical_request, string_to_sign and the Authorization header byte for byte. The x-amz-content-sha256 header is S3-only and is NOT added. Header values are trimmed and inner whitespace collapsed as the suite shows; a header given as a list is the same name repeated on the wire, in that order (joined with commas in the canonical request); a value containing a newline is a folded (multi-line) header value. The session token reaches the signer through the credential: from the request's X-Amz-Security-Token header when present ('post-sts-header-before', signed), else from the case's `session_token` ('get-vanilla-with-session-token', signed without a request header); 'post-sts-header-after' has neither and its token is appended after signing, outside these vectors. Path cases ('normalize-path' group: dot segments, doubled slashes, a raw space, `$`) and query cases (repeated keys ordered by value, empty values, pre-encoded and raw UTF-8 keys, unreserved characters) pin the canonicalization a signer must implement.",
